PROBLEM 3 — REST, CANCEL, BEST PRICES
Reading: 05_ownership_smart_pointers_move.txt
         06_stl_containers.txt
         07_iterators_and_invalidation.txt
================================================================================

Data, private to Orderbook:

  using Level = std::list<Order>;
  std::map<Price, Level, std::greater<Price>> bids_;   // best bid = begin()
  std::map<Price, Level, std::less<Price>>    asks_;   // best ask = begin()
  std::unordered_map<OrderId, Level::iterator> index_; // id -> list node

Behavior for this problem: no order crosses, so add only rests.

  add
    Reject a duplicate id: return an empty vector and do not insert.
    Reject quantity 0 the same way.
    Otherwise append the order to the back of its price level
    (create the level if needed) and store the list iterator in index_.
    Return an empty trade vector.
  cancel
    Unknown id: return false.
    Known id: erase that list node, erase the index entry, erase the
    price level if its list is now empty, return true.
    Canceling the same id twice returns false the second time.
  bestBid / bestAsk
    Empty side: std::nullopt. Otherwise the first key in that map.
  size
    index_.size().

Write these tests before the implementation. Keep the Problem 2 test.

  "cancel removes a resting order"
      Buy 99 x 10, id 1. cancel(1) is true. cancel(1) is false.
      bestBid() is empty. size() is 0.

  "cancel of an unknown id does nothing"

  "the last order at a price removes that level"
      Two buys at 100 (ids 1 and 2). Cancel 1. bestBid() is still 100
      and size() is 1. Cancel 2. bestBid() is empty.

  "duplicate ids are rejected"
      Two adds with id 1. size() is 1. The second add returns no trades.

  "a zero-quantity order is rejected"
      size() stays 0. bestBid() is empty.

  "best bid and best ask are empty on a new book"

