PROBLEM 4 — MATCHING
Reading: 13_architecture_walkthrough.txt, section 5 only
         08_undefined_behavior_case_study.txt (so you do not copy the bug)
================================================================================

Extend add. Incoming quantity that trades is filled against the opposite
side before anything rests.

Loop while the incoming order still has quantity and the opposite side
can trade with it:

  A buy trades while best ask exists and incoming.price >= best ask.
  A sell trades while best bid exists and incoming.price <= best bid.

At the inside level, trade against the front order (oldest) first:

  quantity = min(incoming.remaining, resting.remaining)
  Both remainings decrease by quantity.
  Append a Trade. price is the RESTING order's price.
  buyId is the buyer's id, sellId is the seller's id.
  If the resting order's remaining hits 0, erase it the same way cancel
  does (including dropping an empty level).

After the loop:

  GoodTillCancel with remaining > 0 rests, same as Problem 3.
  FillAndKill never rests. Discard whatever is left.
  If nothing was traded and nothing rested, return an empty vector.
  An order that fully fills does not rest. size() counts resting orders.

Work these by hand before coding. Your tests must match them.

  Example A — full fill at the resting price
    Book: sell id 1, price 100, qty 5.
    Incoming: buy id 2, price 101, qty 5, GoodTillCancel.
    One trade: buy 2, sell 1, price 100, qty 5.
    Book is empty.

  Example B — partial fill, remainder rests
    Book: sell id 1, price 100, qty 5.
    Incoming: buy id 2, price 100, qty 12, GoodTillCancel.
    One trade: price 100, qty 5.
    Book: buy 100 x 7, id 2. bestBid() is 100. bestAsk() is empty.

  Example C — sweep two levels
    Book: sell id 1, price 100, qty 5.
          sell id 2, price 101, qty 10.
    Incoming: buy id 3, price 101, qty 12, GoodTillCancel.
    Trade 1: sell 1, price 100, qty 5.
    Trade 2: sell 2, price 101, qty 7.
    Book: sell 101 x 3, id 2.

  Example D — price-time priority
    Book: sell id 1, price 100, qty 10.   (older)
          sell id 2, price 100, qty 10.
    Incoming: buy id 3, price 100, qty 10.
    The only trade is against id 1.
    Book: sell 100 x 10, id 2.

  Example E — no cross
    Book: sell id 1, price 105, qty 10.
    Incoming: buy id 2, price 100, qty 10.
    No trades. Both rest. bestBid 100, bestAsk 105.

Tests, one per example, plus:

  "a sell hits the best bid and trades at the bid"
    Book: buy 100 x 4, id 1.
    Incoming: sell 99 x 4, id 2.
    Trade price is 100.

